AQE: Adaptive Query Execution
Introduces in Spark 3.0 
It will choose the most efficient query plan during run time
spark.conf.set("spark.sql.adaptive.enabled",true)

Dynamically Coalesce the partitions:
spark default partitions 200: I will simply coalesce partitions. It will reduce shuffle partitions

Optimize the join strategy during Run Time:
Based on data statistics, it will dynamically optimizes query plans at runtime
sort merge join - broad cast join

Dynamically optimizing skewness:
convert skewed partitions into smaller partitions
spark.conf.set("spark.sql.adaptive.skewJoin.enabled", true)
Skewed join problem: When joining two large tables, some keys may have disproportionately more rows than others. 
This causes uneven distribution of work across tasks, leading to performance bottlenecks.

Setting to true: Spark detects skewed partitions during runtime and automatically splits them into smaller chunks.
This balances the workload across tasks and improves query performance.
